[Music]  12 year old singer Evy Claire teared up  after performing a touching tribute to  her late father on night 1 of the  America's Got Talent finale  Andy's dad died earlier this month after  losing his battle with colon cancer how  did you get through that performance I  mean I just prayed before that I would  that I would be able to like that and I  know my dad was there and so I mean from  my family from the audience what was the  significance of that particular song for  this finale that was my dad's favorite  song he'd always sing that and and that  would be the only song he was singing in  public well that my mom would let him  sing in public  yeah that was just kind of like a  tribute to him what hasn't meant not  only to be on this show and competing  and AGT but to share part of it with  your dad to have this great opportunity  with him and memories that we'll never  forget  have you given any thoughts that if you  do take this whole thing home what  you'll do with the million dollars we  had a solid plan before I was gonna use  the money so I go find a better cure for  my dad but now we don't know what to do  events truce maturities arrested  overturned  what you hope to inspire and other kids  who are maybe going through a similar  situation just know that God is on their  side he doesn't abandon us he did these  hard things don't happen because he  doesn't love us he does this because He  loves us he wants to make us stronger he  wants to prepare us for even harder  things down the road even though it  seems like this is the hardest thing  that could possibly happen it's it's  really all just preparation  [Music]

